A||N||5||starter248||Help, '88 2.8 V6 Stall Problems||||1||
Z||000000||starter248||10-19-2000||07:42 AM||||Hi all, newcomer here looking for some help.  I have an 86SE V6 with an 88 Formula engine.  It runs very smooth while crusing but has an intermittent problem with stalling when coming to a stop and resuming travel.  Symptoms are as follows, high idle in park @ 2000rpm and sometimes slows to a rough idle which may be @ 500rpm, when starting off from a complete stop I must let the car "idle" off the line otherwise when you if you give it gas before the car gains enough speed it stalls.  I was  told this could have something to do with the TCC solenoid, however I have disconnected the TCC which I was told should fix this problem but it has not. Interestingly enough the problem occured a couple of times then ceased for several weeks and now it's back and doesn't seem to want to go away. This is a dangerous problem as I could get nailed buy someone when I stall so I would appreciate any suggestions.  Thanks much,<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||07:53 AM||||sounds a bit like a EGR tube leak. someone else should know better as all my work so far has been done on a fiero that isn't running... hehe. ahh well, welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-19-2000||08:11 AM||||Hi,<P>Welcome to the forum.<P>Have you looked at your Throttle Position Sensor (TPS)?  Theogre can give more details on its operation and troubleshooting.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-19-2000||09:25 AM||||Getting any codes?<BR>Need a fuel filter?||||reg||1
Z||000004||LAMBO||10-19-2000||01:44 PM||||My 86 was doing the same exact thing a few days ago. I checked for codes and got code 22. This is the TPS code. Replaced it with a new one and problem solved. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||10-19-2000||07:16 PM||||it sounds like the tps or egr..... check to make sure your egr tubes are hooked up and in good condition, then make sure the actual egr "unit" is working, then if all else fails I would replace the tps.<P>btw, when my egr went south it was idling at like 3k and flooding||||reg||1
